---
import {themes,heritage} from '../../../src/palettes.mjs';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const entries=Object.values(themes);
const origins=[['Silver',heritage.silver],['Light blue',heritage.blueLight],['Heraldic blue',heritage.blue],['Dark blue',heritage.blueDark],['Gold',heritage.gold],['Dark gold',heritage.goldDark],['Light yellow',heritage.yellowLight]];
const keys=['bg','panel','panel2','text','muted','accent','link','selection','success','danger','warning','syntax-keyword','syntax-string','chart-1','chart-2','chart-3'];
const downloads=['martlet.css','martlet.json','martlet-light.css','martlet-dark.css','martlet-light-vscode.json','martlet-dark-vscode.json','martlet-light-terminal.json','martlet-dark-terminal.json'];
---
<BaseLayout>
<section class="hero">
<div class="hero-main"><p class="eyebrow">AN ORIGINAL COLOR THEME</p><h1>Color with a story.<br /><em>Built for what’s next.</em></h1>
<p class="hero-lede">Inspired by the blue, silver, and gold of James P. Howard, II’s personal heraldic identity, Martlet brings a distinctive palette to websites, applications, and readable code.</p>
<div class="actions"><a class="primary" href="#preview">Explore Martlet ↘</a><a class="secondary" href="#downloads">Get the colors</a></div>
<p class="quiet">Open source · Light &amp; dark · Development preview</p></div>
<div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true"><img class="hero-mark" src="/martlet-mark.svg" width="265" height="265" alt="" /><div class="art-label">AZURE · ARGENT · OR</div></div>
</section>
<section id="palette" class="section wrap"><header class="section-header"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / ORIGINS</p><h2>Seven colors. One identity.</h2></div><p>Martlet’s original colors come from James P. Howard, II’s arms and the documented James Howard &amp; Family tartan. The theme adds purpose-built navy surfaces, muted typography, and application-specific colors.</p></header>
<div class="heritage">{origins.map(([name,hex])=><article class="swatch"><div class="chip" style={'background:'+hex}></div><strong>{name}</strong><code>{hex}</code></article>)}</div>
<p class="fineprint">Color provenance: <a href="https://jameshoward.us/2025/05/26/a-new-tartan/">A New Tartan</a>. The historical colors are fixed references; the practical theme colors can improve over time.</p>
</section>
<section id="preview" class="section preview-section"><div class="wrap"><header class="section-header"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / LIVE PREVIEW</p><h2>Two sides of Martlet.</h2></div><p>Light emphasizes crisp white and heraldic blue. Dark pairs midnight navy with gold. Both share the same named color roles.</p></header>
<div class="segmented" role="group" aria-label="Theme preview"><button type="button" data-mode="light" aria-pressed="false">☀ Martlet Light</button><button type="button" data-mode="dark" aria-pressed="true">☾ Martlet Dark</button></div>
<div class="application" data-martlet="dark" id="demo">
<div class="app-bar"><span class="app-name"><img class="app-mark" src="/martlet-mark.svg" width="30" height="30" alt="" /> An imagined application</span><span class="app-links">Overview &nbsp; Projects &nbsp; Settings</span><span class="avatar">JH</span></div>
<div class="app-body"><aside class="sidebar"><small>WORKSPACE</small><strong>▣ &nbsp; Dashboard</strong><span>◫ &nbsp; Projects</span><span>◷ &nbsp; Activity</span><span>⚙ &nbsp; Preferences</span></aside><div class="app-content"><div class="app-heading"><div><small>YOUR WORKSPACE</small><h3>Welcome back.</h3><p>Here's what your projects are doing.</p></div><button type="button">+ New project</button></div>
<div class="stats"><article><small>Active projects</small><strong>12</strong><span>↑ 2 this week</span></article><article><small>Completed tasks</small><strong>248</strong><span>↑ 18 this week</span></article><article><small>Outstanding reviews</small><strong>03</strong><span>Needs attention</span></article></div>
<div class="code-example"><header>theme.mjs <span>● ● ●</span></header><pre><code><i>const</i> theme = &#123;
  <mark>name</mark>: <em>'Martlet'</em>,
  <mark>mode</mark>: <em>'dark'</em>,
  <mark>accessible</mark>: <i>true</i>,
  <mark>version</mark>: <u>1</u>
&#125;;</code></pre></div></div></div>
</div><p class="fineprint">This is an illustrative mockup, not a Prism 7 screenshot. Its colors are drawn from the generated Martlet CSS.</p></div></section>
<section id="tokens" class="section wrap"><header class="section-header"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / DESIGN TOKENS</p><h2>Beyond a simple palette.</h2></div><p>88 semantic tokens in each mode describe interface surfaces, text, controls, statuses, charts, and source code. The complete specification is machine-readable.</p></header>
<div class="comparison">{entries.map(theme=><article class="token-card"><h3>{theme.name}</h3>{keys.map(k=><div class="token-row"><div class="token-chip" style={'background:'+theme.tokens[k]}></div><div><strong>{k}</strong><small>--martlet-{k}</small></div><code>{theme.tokens[k]}</code></div>)}</article>)}</div>
<p class="fineprint">Automated contrast tests cover selected text/background combinations; full accessibility evaluation remains part of the release work.</p>
</section>
<section class="section example-section"><div class="wrap example-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">04 / IMPLEMENTATION</p><h2>Made to travel.</h2><p>Scoped CSS variables mean Martlet can live alongside another application's styles, or even render Light and Dark in separate components on the same page.</p><p>Starter exports also cover sixteen terminal colors and VS Code syntax roles.</p></div>
<pre><code>&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="martlet.css"&gt;

&lt;main data-martlet="dark"&gt;
  &lt;article class="panel"&gt;Hello, Martlet.&lt;/article&gt;
&lt;/main&gt;

/* Your stylesheet */
.panel &#123;
  background: var(--martlet-panel);
  color: var(--martlet-text);
&#125;</code></pre></div></section>
<section id="downloads" class="section wrap"><header class="section-header"><div><p class="eyebrow">05 / DOWNLOAD</p><h2>Pick up the palette.</h2></div><p>All files are generated from one canonical source. These are development artifacts, not final polished application extensions.</p></header><div class="download-grid">{downloads.map(name=><a href={'/downloads/'+name} download><span><strong>{name.startsWith('martlet-light')?'Martlet Light':name.startsWith('martlet-dark')?'Martlet Dark':'Complete Martlet'} </strong><small>{name}</small></span><span class="arrow">↓</span></a>)}</div>
<p class="fineprint">First implemented in <a href="https://prism7.app/">Prism 7</a>. Source repository: <a href="https://github.com/k3jph/martlettheme">k3jph/martlettheme</a>.</p></section>

<script>
const preview=document.getElementById('demo');
const buttons=[...document.querySelectorAll('button[data-mode]')];
for(const b of buttons) b.addEventListener('click',()=>{
  preview?.setAttribute('data-martlet',b.getAttribute('data-mode')||'dark');
  buttons.forEach(other=>other.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(other===b)));
});
</script>
</BaseLayout>
